T359 / F-T359-1 — HANDED OVER AS A DIFF, NOT APPLIED. `nexus/` is out of this review's scope.

WHAT IT DOES, AND WHY IT IS NOT A DECISION I MAY MAKE
-----------------------------------------------------
This is the one-line change that turns T352's `HARNESS-ERROR` into a graded `FAIL`. It is
NOT a fix to be merged on my say-so: whether the port's residue refusal is an "I cannot
answer" (error) or an "I refuse, and that refusal is the answer" (Refusal) is exactly the
question G-19 puts to Buyan. Option (a) — the port's refusal is CORRECT and stands, recorded
as a deliberate named deviation — implies this routing, because a deliberate deviation must
be GRADEABLE. Option (b) implies deleting the refusal instead. So this patch lands only if
(a) is chosen, and the HTTP status and code below are placeholders a real change must settle.

It was applied ONLY in a throwaway /tmp copy of the repo, to MEASURE the claim in F-T359-1.
Evidence: `schema-drive/runD-patched.log` — with this change and T352's candidate vector
BYTE-IDENTICAL (`amount_minor: "10013"` untouched), the run reports

    LDG-T352-CANDIDATE-residue-3dp  parity  ledger_rest_posting  FAIL  1 cells (0 money)
        the implementation REFUSED a request the oracle ACCEPTED (HTTP 422 …): ledger:
        monetary text "100.125000" carries sub-minor-unit residue at scale 2 …
    ledger parity  PASS 7  FAIL 1
    ledger harness errors  0
    EXIT=1

i.e. the divergence grades as a definite, reproducible red with NO schema change whatsoever
— which is the whole of F-T359-1.

