WHAT MUST BE SETTLED BEFORE THIS IS MERGED, none of it mine to settle:

  1. G-19 option (a) ratified by Buyan. Under (b) this patch is wrong and the refusal goes
     away entirely.
  2. The HTTP status and code. 422 / "ledger.residue.refused" are invented by me for the
     measurement. This is a PORT-ORIGINATED refusal with no oracle counterpart, so it needs
     its own namespace convention — the existing refusal codes are all oracle codes
     transcribed from captures, and reusing that shape would make a port invention look like
     an oracle observation.
  3. Whether the port should refuse an amount the oracle emitted at all, versus refusing only
     an amount a CALLER supplied. The two directions are not the same question and DEC-2 §4.3
     consequence 2 as written does not separate them.
  4. The vector to promote alongside it, which needs the `amount_minor` sentinel from
     F-T359-1 — otherwise its author is still forced to write a fiction, and `10013` in the
     store is worse than no vector.
  5. `EXEMPTION_PIN_LEDGER_PARITY` / `_REFUSAL` / `_MONEYCELLS` at `.softhouse/conformance.sh:681-683`
     move in the same commit as any promoted vector (compared by `-eq` at `:3469-3471`).
